# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
# The rule above is anchored to the root, so the audit renderer's own
# dependencies — 200MB of Playwright and Express, installed to run it locally —
# were showing up as untracked files waiting to be committed by accident.
seo-audit-tool/renderer/node_modules/
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# CMS update packages built by `npm run cms:release` — shipped, not committed
/releases/

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
!.env.example
# The QA harness's credentials template is committed by design (qa/README.md).
!qa/.env.qa.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# claude code — local machine settings
.claude/settings.local.json

# markdown — dev notes / working docs only (README, CLAUDE, handoffs,
# templates, copy/pricing change logs). The website ships no .md; all
# content is .mdx, which this pattern does NOT match. Kept out of the
# repo so loose working files never get committed again.
*.md

# Exception: the audit engine documents itself.
#
# These are not loose notes. They are the only record of how that subsystem is
# installed on a server, why each of its 33 checks is written the way it is, and
# what its tests are guarding — and the engine now runs in two places that have
# to stay in agreement. Kept out of the repo, that knowledge lives nowhere.
#
# The engine never reaches production regardless: `.github/workflows/deploy.yml`
# removes `seo-audit-tool/` before the deploy branch is built, so nothing here
# adds weight to the Plesk docroot.
!seo-audit-tool/**/*.md
# Claude Code skills are instructions, not dev notes — version them.
!.claude/skills/**/*.md
# Hand-off notes for the Planner (how a CMS feature is applied to the sites).
!docs/planner/
!docs/planner/*.md
# The entry point for agents and people opening the base.
!/START_HERE.md
# Sources of the end-user PDF guides (docs/user-guides/_build rebuilds them).
!/docs/user-guides/src/*.md
# Technical manuals for developers working on the CMS.
!/docs/dev-guides/*.md

# audit / analytics exports — Google Search Console + Screaming Frog reports.
# Working artifacts, not build inputs; they hold crawl/analytics data and must
# never ride the deploy branch into the Plesk docroot. Scoped to the report
# folders and GSC's export naming so the tracked logo.zip is left untouched.
google search console report/
frog reports/
praion.gr-*.zip

# CMS local media uploads
.data/

# Local database snapshots — never committed.
backups/

# Build dirs of the other instances that share this checkout: the agents' dev
# server (npm run dev:qa) and a production build run with NEXT_DIST_DIR set, so
# verifying a build never disturbs a running dev server. tsconfig.json already
# lists their generated route types.
.next-qa/
.next-build/
.next-wrongdb-test/

# QA harness — the suite's source is committed, its output and local state
# is not: installed deps, the studio's SQLite, captured screenshots/videos,
# Playwright's own report dirs, and the saved browser sessions (real
# credentials/cookies for the local admin).
qa/node_modules/
qa/artifacts/
qa/playwright-report/
qa/test-results/
qa/results.json
qa/.auth/

# The Agent Studio app is delivered by its bundle rather than authored here, so
# most of it stays out. Two exceptions:
#
#   data/     the reports it wrote — the record of what was audited.
#   server/   the part that actually runs the agents, and the part we now patch.
#             A fix there stopped the harness reporting "no confirmed bugs" for a
#             run that never happened (F-049). Leaving that untracked would lose
#             it on the next machine and quietly restore a harness that reports
#             success for zero work. Once we maintain a file, it belongs in git.
#
# `web/` and `node_modules/` are still the bundle's business.
qa/studio/*
!qa/studio/data/
!qa/studio/server/
qa/studio/data/studio.db
qa/studio/node_modules/

# Local-only downloads: the agent-studio drop and a pulled-down env file
# (the latter holds live secrets — never commit it).
agent-studio-bundle.zip
env.download
.history/
.data/

# SEO/AEO audit engine — the build artefacts only.
#
# The engine itself is TRACKED: it is the source of the `deploy-api` branch, so
# a check class that git cannot see is a check that never reaches the server.
# What must stay out is everything the tooling generates inside that folder —
# a full Laravel install's vendor/, the renderer's node_modules, and any .env
# a local run leaves behind. This used to be a blanket `seo-audit-tool/`, which
# ignored new engine sources just as effectively as it ignored the junk.
seo-audit-tool/**/vendor/
seo-audit-tool/**/node_modules/
seo-audit-tool/**/.env
seo-audit-tool/laravel/storage/
seo-audit-tool/laravel/bootstrap/cache/
seo-audit-tool/**/*.log
